  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture on the Mac, with the LOT-001 (#38) kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), what the multi-quote cookie holds. `W14`'s metadata records only its name, `quoteshardwarefr-prive-<post>`, not its value or expiry. LOT-049 needs to know whether HFR clears the selection itself after a post, or whether the client must.\n\n### Scope\n\n- The `Set-Cookie` of a multi-quote selection, as in `W14`: record the value **shape** (redacted to a placeholder that keeps its structure) and the expiry or `Max-Age`.\n- After a reply posted with that selection, record whether HFR's answer expires or rewrites the cookie.\n- Never commit a real cookie value. The meta records the names and the shape only (FIXTURES.md).\n\nRules: anonymize every free-text field. Never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36). One PR per batch of captures.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nLOT-049 (#75, quote engine), and through it LOT-086 (#178, multi-quote in the composer).\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Owner / session\n\n— (ready; `host: mac`)\n\n### Source\n\nLOT-049 issue body (steward rewrite, 2026-10-29): no legacy code clears the cookie after a post. Restart plan on #166.",
